 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? It' an effect called color fading. Acrylic paints dry on top of the paper, so the color doesn't deepen. You can partially overcome it with several thin layers. You can spot it with a dry layer. Hold it up and see how the color looks from few inches away. If it looks like it needs more, go for it. Use a glossy medium first, like ink or a thick gel pen. Then build up clear top coats. At each layer, wipe off the brush and wipe around the tip before you start, so there's no nicks that show up as little nicks.",
